name: Local Services
description: A site for a local trade, such as a plumber, built around a request-a-quote form.
tags: [local-business]
defaultLanguage: en

# Foundation to use for this site
foundation: foundation

# Homepage - specifies which page folder becomes the root route (/)
index: home

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the quote form sends submissions — the `submit` service.
#
# Until it has somewhere to send them, the form on the homepage renders DISABLED
# with a short explanation instead of collecting answers it cannot deliver. That
# is the intended behaviour, not a broken template: a form posting into an
# endpoint that does not exist loses what a visitor typed and looks like it
# worked.
#
# `submit: true` asks your host for its form service, where it offers one. To
# use an endpoint of your own instead, give its address — a relative path is
# resolved against the site's `base:`, and an absolute URL works for a form
# service on another origin:
#
#   submit: /forms
#   submit: https://forms.example.com/intake
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
services:
  submit: true

# Build options
build:
  prerender: true
